      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It creates a `Tag` with empty name and namespace, calls `textState()` (which returns `null` for tags without `RcData`/`Data` options), and asserts the tag is not known. Let me write a clearer version.Now I'll compile-check the test.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version replaces the cryptic `test30()` method name with `test_directlyConstructedTagWithEmptyNameIsUnknownAndHasNoTextState()`, uses a descriptive variable name `emptyTag`, and adds a Javadoc comment and inline comments explaining why `textState()` returns null and why `isKnownTag()` is expected to be false — all without changing the runtime behavior."
